    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{x^2}{9}-\\dfrac{y^2}{4}=1$.",
      "worked": "Use $\\sec^2t-\\tan^2t=1$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sec t&=\\frac{x}{3},\\qquad \\tan t=\\frac{y}{2}\\\\\\left(\\frac{x}{3}\\right)^2-\\left(\\frac{y}{2}\\right)^2&=1\\\\\\frac{x^2}{9}-\\frac{y^2}{4}&=1\\end{align*}$$",
